{"kind":"stack","id":"s1","title":"Dissolving and recovering substances","theme":{"background":"#f4faf7","foreground":"#1d3b2f","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Dissolving"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"When a solid mixes into a liquid and seems to disappear, it has dissolved. The liquid is then called a solution."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-q","content":"Which of these will dissolve in water?"},{"type":"button","id":"c2-a","label":"Sugar","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Sand","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-c","label":"Pebbles","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"What do we call the liquid formed when a solid dissolves?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"A solution","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"A mixture of solids","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"A gas","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-t","content":"You have a cup of salty water. You want the salt back. What do you do first?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Heat the water to evaporate it","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Pour the water down the sink","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"Good choice. The water turns to vapour and the salt is left behind in the cup."},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"The salt is lost down the drain. To get it back, you should have evaporated the water."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"Evaporation"},{"type":"text","id":"c7-e","content":"Evaporation is when a liquid is heated and turns into vapour, leaving any dissolved solid behind."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"Which method gets salt back from salty water?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"Evaporating the water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Pouring the water away","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"Shaking the cup","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Does sugar dissolve faster in warm water or cold water?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"Warm water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Cold water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which of these is a solution?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"Salt mixed fully into water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Sand mixed into water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Oil floating on water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-q","content":"Which material does not dissolve in water?"},{"type":"button","id":"c11-a","label":"Sand","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c12"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c11-b","label":"Salt","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c12"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c11-c","label":"Sugar","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c12"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c12","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c12-q","content":"After evaporating salty water, what is left in the cup?"},{"type":"button","id":"c12-a","label":"Salt crystals","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c13"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c12-b","label":"Nothing at all","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c13"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c12-c","label":"Liquid water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c13"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c13","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c13-h","content":"Well done, you finished the dissolving lesson!"},{"type":"text","id":"c13-m","content":"You now know which materials dissolve and how to get a solid back from a solution. Keep exploring!"}],"actions":[]}}
